# Secrets. Matched by PATTERN, never by exact filename.
#
# An exact-name list is how one .gmail-refresh-<name> file got swept into a commit: the
# list was written before the Gmail mint existed, so the new file simply was
# not covered. GitHub push protection caught it. Patterns cover files that do
# not exist yet.
*refresh*token*
.gmail-refresh*
.yt-refresh*
*client_secret*.json
*.token
.cf-token
.bot-token
.eventsub-secret
.vod-webhook-token
*.pem
*.key

# Working files
_tmp_*.mp4
__pycache__/
*.pyc
